("Scroll of the Heroes' Table", "Scroll", "Very Rare", None, "As a Magic action, you read this scroll aloud to cast Heroes' Feast, without material components. The scroll then turns to dust."),
("Scroll of the Sealed Tomb", "Scroll", "Legendary", None, "As a Magic action, you read this scroll aloud and point at a creature you can see within 30 feet. You cast Imprisonment (save DC 19) on it, without material components, and you can choose only the Burial, Chaining, or Slumber form. The scroll then turns to dust."),
# ================= AMMUNITION =================
("Dreamthorn Needle", "Ammunition", "Uncommon", None, "On a hit, this blowgun needle forces the target to make a DC 13 Constitution save. On a failed save, its Speed is 0 and it has the Incapacitated condition until the end of its next turn. If the target has 20 Hit Points or fewer after the hit, it instead has the Unconscious condition for 1 minute, or until it takes damage or someone takes an action to wake it. Found in bundles of 1d4."),
("Bolt of the Reversed Fall", "Ammunition", "Rare", None, "On a hit, a Large or smaller target makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failed save, it rises 20 feet into the air and floats there for 1 minute, as if from the Levitate spell. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success and floating gently to the ground."),
("Arrow of Withering", "Ammunition", "Rare", None, "On a hit, the target takes an extra 3d6 Necrotic damage, and its Hit Point maximum is reduced by the same amount until it finishes a Long Rest. The arrow then crumbles to ash."),
("Arrow of the Ninefold Rain", "Ammunition", "Very Rare", None, "When you fire this arrow at a point within the weapon's normal range, it splits into nine arrows. Make a separate attack roll against each of up to nine creatures of your choice within 20 feet of that point. Each arrow deals 2d10 Piercing damage on a hit. The arrows then vanish."),
("Bolt of the Stone Gaze", "Ammunition", "Very Rare", None, "On a hit, the target makes a DC 17 Constitution save, as if it were the target of the Flesh to Stone spell, and the effect doesn't require Concentration. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns as the spell says, and it is Petrified for good only after three failed saves. Greater Restoration ends the effect as usual. The bolt then turns to grey dust."),
("Arrow of the Last Word", "Ammunition", "Legendary", None, "When you hit a creature with this arrow, and the creature has 100 Hit Points or fewer after the damage, it dies, as if from the Power Word Kill spell. A creature with more than 100 Hit Points after the damage is not affected. On a miss, nothing happens. Either way, the arrow then vanishes."),
